  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Assay Register",
    "overview": "A flat, quiet register built on the Interfere design system (design.interfere.com). Interfere supplies the material: Radix colour scales with hue-free neutrals, Inter for the interface, a mono for figures, and hairline shadow rings in place of borders. The product supplies the one thing that is its own: the hallmark, one small stamp per independent auditor on every mint, read left to right like marks on a bar of metal.\n\nSurfaces are a light grey shell with white containers in light mode, and black with a near-black container in dark mode. Depth comes from 0.5px rings, grey alpha fills and one quiet light from above (the top-lit sheen), never from colour or blur. Hue is spent on state: green, orange and tomato for health, and Interfere blue (#0090ff) only for focus, info badges and one chart series. Everything else is grey and ink. The UI is deliberately restrained; glass styling is rejected outright, and the only gradients outside the brand are the sheen's grey ones.\n\nThe visual system is adapted from Interfere. Earlier layout inspiration came from Umbrel; no Umbrel code is used (Umbrel is PolyForm Noncommercial).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Inter Variable with 'ss03' for all interface text; TX-02 with 'ss02' only for figures, URLs, codes and stamps.",
      "Hue-free grey neutrals expressed as alpha steps (gray-a3 to gray-a12), so they sit on any surface.",
      "One brand hue (#0090ff), used sparingly.",
      "Hairline \"shadow-default\" rings instead of borders; 0.5px rules between rows.",
      "One quiet light from above: panels and controls lightest at the top, fields pressed in.",
      "Primary actions are inverted: near-black in light, near-white in dark.",
      "The hallmark row is the signature: Interfere md badges in four verdict states.",
      "Light and dark themes are first-class, switched from a sun/moon icon at the top right and set before first paint."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Grey Is Hue-Free Rule",
        "body": "Neutrals are pure greys as alpha steps. No warm or cool tint, no cream, no tinted paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State-Only Hue Rule",
        "body": "Green, orange and tomato appear only when the system reports a health state, a verdict or an error category. Navigation, headings and surfaces stay grey.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sparing Blue Rule",
        "body": "#0090ff is for focus, selection, info badges and one chart series. It is never a button fill, a heading colour or a surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Inverted Primary Rule",
        "body": "The main action is the inverse of the page: near-black in light mode, near-white in dark mode. It is not blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Inter for words, TX-02 for values. Never set prose, headings or buttons in TX-02, and never set a figure, URL or code in Inter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Plain Zero Rule",
        "body": "Every TX-02 run carries 'ss02' and tabular numerals, so 0 never reads as a dotted or slashed glyph and columns align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Not Border Rule",
        "body": "Containers get a 0.5px ring, not a CSS border. Real borders exist only as 0.5px row rules.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Top-Lit Rule",
        "section": "elevation",
        "body": "One light, from above, the same everywhere: raised things are lightest at the top, wells are shaded under their top edge. The sheen is grey and quiet (a few percent, never a visible band of colour), never on state colour, and nothing glows. Added 2026-10-30 at the owner's request, after Umbrel's dark UI (the idea only; no Umbrel code)."
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Glass Rule",
        "body": "No backdrop blur, no translucent glass panels, no glow, and no gradients but the sheen's and the brand's.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set interface text in InterVariable with 'ss03', and figures, URLs, codes and stamps in TX-02 with 'ss02' and tabular numerals.",
      "Do use the alpha grey tokens (`--fg`, `--fg-2`, `--fg-3`, `--component`, `--border`) so surfaces work in both themes.",
      "Do separate containers with the hairline ring and rows with 0.5px `--border` rules.",
      "Do light raised panels and controls from above and press fields in, with the `--sheen-*` and `--s-*` tokens, in both themes.",
      "Do make the primary action inverted (`--inverted` / `--on-inverted`).",
      "Do keep status colour tied to a real state: success, warning (Radix orange), danger (tomato).",
      "Do draw every auditor verdict as a hallmark in one of its four states.",
      "Do keep the header, pages and footer on the shared 960px column."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use glass, backdrop blur, glow or coloured gradients; the owner regards them as AI slop. The grey top-lit sheen and the brand's metal are the only gradients.",
      "Don't tint the neutrals warm or cool, or reintroduce cream fills or amber status.",
      "Don't use #0090ff as a button fill, heading colour or decoration.",
      "Don't add CSS borders to cards or fields; use the hairline shadow.",
      "Don't set prose, headings or buttons in TX-02.",
      "Don't lift elements with large drop shadows; shadow-large is for overlays only."
    ]
  }
}
